From: STD Team <std@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] STD: hook select_task_rq

Hook select_task_rq via std_select_cpu. Keeps routing above deadline
with no new class. Respects affinity and small-system guard.
Placement stays at wakeup time; the pick path is untouched so the
disabled cost is zero.

Signed-off-by: STD Team <std@kernel.org>
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -3634,6 +3634,13 @@
 
 	if (p->nr_cpus_allowed > 1 && !is_migration_disabled(p)) {
 		cpu = p->sched_class->select_task_rq(p, cpu, *wake_flags);
+		/*
+		 * STD routing shim above deadline: steer toward the
+		 * preferred CPU group while honoring affinity. Stop
+		 * tasks are never intercepted. Placement stays at
+		 * wakeup time; the pick path is untouched.
+		 */
+		cpu = std_select_cpu(p, cpu);
 		*wake_flags |= WF_RQ_SELECTED;
 	} else {
 		cpu = cpumask_any(p->cpus_ptr);
